Z||000000||lennyb4||04-07-2000||09:49 AM||||OK guys, i want to re-paint my fiero the same color as it is (med. burgendy w/metal flake). The only problem is i've never painted a car before..HELP  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">... I'm sure some of you have painted either your car or helped before. Any pointers or tips. I'm just worried it will come out looking like bubble wrap or something  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> (orange peel, etc.).||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||04-07-2000||10:22 AM||||Do the prep yourself and then take it to Macco. Cheapest and easiest way out<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||04-07-2000||11:01 AM||||I would say take it to a paint shop. Todays paint are not easy to use and you need a lot of equipment. Unless you have done some painting in the past and know how to use a sprayer and you hava a mask, protective clothing, a compressor, sanding equipment. N ot to say that you can't do it. But you start by sanding then special primers are required, once prepped properly then you start out spraying your base coat making that you have no runs. Finally you spray the clearcoat and when that is dry then you go to what we call color sanding and then the final buffing. OH! yea I forgot something. All the masking and tape making sure that everything is covered correctly so as to not hve overspray all over other parts of the car that are going to be painted. ie all the glass. Sorry for the long post but that ia why I have a professional painter work for me. He knows what he is doing. I have painted a lot of cars myself but no more.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||04-07-2000||11:08 AM||||I have a guy down my way who does a wonderful job for $1200.00 OTD. He works out of a one car garage in Jeromsville. He just recently painted my car and Tabascos car and they both came out great. Maybe not show car quality but close. He had my car for about a week and a half total. His price included all prep and trim work. ||||reg||14
Z||000004||lennyb4||04-07-2000||11:10 AM||||I knew there would be alot of work involved, maybe i will strip all exterior/trim/lights off the car and them trailer it up to macco or someone. I guess i just want a nice paint job w/o spending alot of money that i dont have...hmmmm..could always sell the wife and kids..hehehe...any bids?||||reg||14
Z||000005||86SE||04-07-2000||06:10 PM||||My older brother is painting my car for me in a few weeks.  All I have to do is help him sand it!!  He's not charging me for labor, just paint and clearcoat!!  We figure about $70 for ferrari yellow paint and $50 for very clear clearcoat.<BR>They mix their own paint at the shop so paint isnt so expensive.  I just have to drive it from Sioux Falls, SD to Omaha, NE.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Old Lar||04-07-2000||08:22 PM||||I used to do some painting with lacquor paint and it was fun, dried fast and you could sand out your mistakes.  The metallics were a pain to get the flakes to lay down the same.  I saw some nice Macco $700 paint jobs in Florida.  Preparation is everything.  If I were to do it and wanted a good job, I'd remove all the body panels and paint them off the car.  Then you can do all the black frame components.  It would be time consuming.  I've had the noses done on both my cars, the noses were painted off the car.||||reg||1
